  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">PDO Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increase of agriculture productivity for crops</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2012-12-01" value="0.00" year="2012">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">The baseline data was established by randomly selecting 48 beneficiaries (12 per District) from farmers that were selected in thesessions 1 to 5 (same ones than in No. 1).</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2012-12-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2014-12-08"></period-end>
     <target value="5.00"></target>
     <actual value="-16.90">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Statistics show a dismal 16.9% decrease in crop production due to poor environmental conditions, difficulty in finding labor, pestand diseases affecting the major crops. To measure productivity, it needs several years between baseline and end line, but in thiscase it was less than a year.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">PDO Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increase of agriculture incomes of small farmers</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2012-12-01" value="0.00" year="2012">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">The baseline was established by random selection of 48 beneficiaries (12 per district) from farmers that were selected in sessions1 to 5.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2012-12-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2014-12-08"></period-end>
     <target value="5.00"></target>
     <actual value="24.60">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Data obtained from farmer interviews showed a noteworthy achievement of a 24.57% average increase in the estimated agriculturalyearly income of the 48 randomly selected farmers. Overall, agriculture income disaggregated by district shows that farmer incomein all districts improved. This surpassed the target value by 19.57%. However, the income of 33.3% of the farmers remained thesame. Thisoccurred due to a number of external factors related to market and labor. Agriculture income is not seen as a goodindicator for such a project, mostly because it was measured after just one planting season.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
